INSERT INTO blog_post_translations
  (post_id, locale, slug, title, excerpt, body_html, seo_title, seo_description)
VALUES (
  :post_id, 'en', $x$how-to-top-up-xbox-from-uzbekistan$x$,
  $x$How to top up Xbox from Uzbekistan$x$,
  $x$How to top up Xbox from Uzbekistan: your Microsoft account's country, the three-month rule for changing region, which gift card to buy and how to redeem it.$x$,
$x$<p>You top up Xbox with a gift card from the country set on your Microsoft account. Check your account's country, buy a card for that country and redeem the code on the console or on Microsoft's website.</p>
<h2>Key takeaways</h2>
<ul>
<li>An Xbox card works only on an account of the same country. Microsoft does not change a card's region, not even through support.</li>
<li>You can change your Microsoft account's country, but not more than once in three months.</li>
<li>Money in your balance does not move with a country change. Spend it first.</li>
<li>Keep the console's store region the same as the account's.</li>
<li>YuPay has Xbox cards for 21 countries. You pay in soʻm with Click, Payme or Uzum. The total in soʻm is shown before payment, and that is exactly what is charged.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Account country and console region</h2>
<p>Xbox has two settings that people often mix up.</p>
<p><strong>Microsoft account country.</strong> It sets your balance currency and which cards will work. You can see it in your Microsoft account profile, under &quot;Your info&quot;.</p>
<p><strong>Console region.</strong> This is a setting on the console itself: Settings → System → Language &amp; location. It decides which store you see. Keep it the same as the account country, or the store and your balance will disagree.</p>
<p>Players in Uzbekistan usually use an account from another country: the USA, Turkey, the UAE, Poland. Which country is your choice. What matters is that you then top it up with cards of that same country.</p>
<h2>How to change your Xbox region</h2>
<p>If the account was created for the wrong country, you can change it. Microsoft's rules:</p>
<ol>
<li>You cannot change the country if you already changed it in the last three months.</li>
<li>Money in your balance does not move to the new region. Spend it before switching.</li>
<li>Some subscriptions and purchases may not work in the new region. Check this first, especially if you have an active subscription.</li>
<li>After changing the account country, change the console region in Language &amp; location as well.</li>
</ol>
<p>Because of the three-month rule, do not switch country for a single discount. Pick a region once and keep topping it up.</p>
<h2>Which card to buy</h2>
<p>One rule: a card from the same country as your account. A US card will not redeem on a Turkish account, and the other way round. Microsoft support cannot move a card to another region, so a wrong purchase cannot be fixed later.</p>
<p>The <a href="/en/store/xbox">YuPay catalogue</a> has one Xbox page with a country switcher. For example:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/en/store/xbox?region=us">Xbox USA</a> — for a US account;</li>
<li><a href="/en/store/xbox?region=tr">Xbox Turkey</a> — for a Turkish one;</li>
<li><a href="/en/store/xbox?region=ae">Xbox UAE</a> — for a UAE account;</li>
<li><a href="/en/store/xbox?region=pl">Xbox Poland</a> — for a Polish one.</li>
</ul>
<p>There are also the UK, Germany, Spain, Brazil, Mexico, Canada, Japan and others. Take the &quot;EU&quot; card only if your account's country is in the euro zone.</p>
<h2>How to redeem an Xbox card</h2>
<p>After payment, the code appears on the order page and arrives by e-mail. You can redeem it in two ways.</p>
<p><strong>On the console:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Sign in to the right profile.</li>
<li>Open Microsoft Store.</li>
<li>Press the menu button and choose &quot;Redeem&quot;.</li>
<li>Enter the 25-character code and confirm.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>On the web:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Open the redeem page on Microsoft's website (microsoft.com/redeem).</li>
<li>Sign in to the same Microsoft account you use on the console.</li>
<li>Enter the code and confirm.</li>
</ol>
<p>The money goes to your account balance. The code is single-use: once redeemed, it will not work again.</p>
<h2>Games and Game Pass from your balance</h2>
<p>The balance is spent in Microsoft Store: on games, add-ons, in-game currency and a Game Pass subscription. At checkout, choose to pay from your account balance.</p>
<p>If you are short of the amount you need, add another card of the same country. Balances add up.</p>
<p>Grand Theft Auto VI came out on 19 November 2026, including on Xbox Series X|S. According to Rockstar, Xbox codes are not region-locked. The simplest route is to buy the game in your account's Microsoft Store from your balance. Details are in our guide on <a href="/en/blog/how-to-buy-gta-6-in-uzbekistan">how to buy GTA 6 in Uzbekistan</a>.</p>
<h2>Redeem errors</h2>
<p>If a code is not accepted, Xbox shows an error, often with a code like &quot;PUR-…&quot;. In plain words there are three causes.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Wrong account.</strong> You are signed in to another profile, or to another Microsoft account on the website. Check the account's e-mail.</li>
<li><strong>Wrong region.</strong> The card's country does not match the account's. This is a common cause. The only fix is changing the account country, within the three-month rule.</li>
<li><strong>The code is already redeemed or mistyped.</strong> Check the characters: letters and digits are easy to confuse. Look at the account's order history: the money may already be in your balance.</li>
</ul>
<p>If everything matches and the code still fails, contact YuPay support with the order number.</p>
<h2>Summary</h2>
<p>Find your Microsoft account's country, get a card for that country and redeem it on the console or on the website. Change region rarely: once in three months and only with an empty balance.</p>
<p>The card you need is in the <a href="/en/store/xbox">Xbox section of the YuPay catalogue</a>. PlayStation works in a similar way; see our guide on <a href="/en/blog/how-to-buy-ps-store-games-from-uzbekistan">how to buy PS Store games from Uzbekistan</a>.</p>$x$,
  $x$How to top up Xbox from Uzbekistan — gift cards and region$x$,
  $x$Top up Xbox from Uzbekistan: a gift card of your Microsoft account's country, region change once in three months, redeeming the code and PUR errors. Pay in soʻm.$x$
);

